{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.not_ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.not_ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume.lean#L120-L127","doc":"**The identity is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nWith no hyperbolic pieces the sum is empty, so a nonzero observable fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_volumes_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_volumes_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume.lean#L103-L118","doc":"**The vanishing-volume case, derived**: pieces present but all of zero\nThurston volume ⇒ the observable vanishes.\n\nThe other reading of the same sentence in the `.md`. Stated separately\nbecause an empty piece set and a set of volume-zero pieces are different\ngeometric situations that happen to share a conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_no_hyperbolic_pieces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_no_hyperbolic_pieces","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume.lean#L89-L101","doc":"**The Seifert-fibered case, derived**: no hyperbolic piece ⇒ the\nobservable vanishes.\n\nThe `.md`'s *\"pure-rotation 3-cycles trace Heegaard torus trajectories,\nleaving a Seifert-fibered complement where `V_hyp = 0`\"* — obtained from the\ngraded sum rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/ReebBundleComplementEqualsVolume.lean#L76-L87","doc":"**The claim of `prop:reeb-bundle-complement-equals-volume`**, as a\nproposition over caller-supplied data:\n\n    tr_M(ρ(β)) = Σ_{P_i ∈ hyperbolicPieces} ρ_F(P_i) · V_hyp(P_i).\n\n**Named, not asserted**, and conditional on `conj:mass-volume-factorization`.\nThe sum is explicit rather than collapsed into one scalar — see the module\ndocstring for why that distinction is the proposition's content. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:reeb-bundle-complement-equals-volume","label":"prop:reeb-bundle-complement-equals-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-bundle-complement-equals-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}